IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap6-s2031`

-- TESTS for snap6-s2031.l4 (section 2031, Minnesota Family Investment Project).
-- Every expected value is written here from the text quoted above the assertion, before the module was run.
-- JUST FALSE = "the text says no in its own words"; NOTHING = "not covered"; JUST TRUE = "the text says yes".


§ `Tests of section 2031`

§§ `(a) In general`
-- src:2845 | (2) The Project may be implemented only in accordance with this section and only if the Secretary of Health and Human Services approves an application submitted by the State permitting the State to include in the Project families who are eligible to receive benefits under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act.
-- (a)(2): not in accordance with this section, or the Secretary of Health and Human Services does not approve: "only" bars.
#ASSERT `s 2031(a)(2) the Project may be implemented` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(a)(2) the Project may be implemented` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(a)(2) the Project may be implemented` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- in accordance and approved, or approval not supplied: "only" grants nothing.
#ASSERT `s 2031(a)(2) the Project may be implemented` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(a)(2) the Project may be implemented` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2844 | (1) Subject to paragraph (2), upon written application of the State of Minnesota that complies with this section and sections 6 to 11, 13, 130, and 132 of article 5 of 282 of the 1989 Laws of Minnesota, and after approval of such application by the Secretary in accordance with subsections (b) and (d), the State may implement a family investment demonstration project (hereinafter in this section referred to as the “Project”) in parts of the State to determine whether the Project more effectively helps families to become self-supporting and enhances their ability to care for their children than do the supplemental nutrition assistance program and programs under parts A and F [Footnote: 1 See References in Text note below.] of title IV of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.]. The State may provide cash payments under the Project, subject to paragraph (2), that replace assistance otherwise available under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act.
-- (a)(1): a complying application, approved, and (2) does not bar.
#ASSERT `s 2031(a)(1) the State may implement the Project` TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(a)(1) the State may implement the Project` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Subject to paragraph (2)": a bar by (2) carries.
#ASSERT `s 2031(a)(1) the State may implement the Project` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no complying application, or no approval by the Secretary: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 2031(a)(1) the State may implement the Project` FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(a)(1) the State may implement the Project` TRUE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(a)(1) the State may implement the Project` TRUE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(b) Required terms and conditions of Project`
-- src:2847 | The application submitted by the State under subsection (a) shall provide an assurance that the Project shall satisfy all of the following requirements:
#ASSERT `s 2031(b) the application complies with the requirements specified in subsection (b)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b) the application complies with the requirements specified in subsection (b)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2848 | (1) Only families may be eligible to receive assistance and services through the Project.
-- (b)(1): a group that is not a family may not be eligible; a family is not granted anything here.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(1) the group may be eligible to receive assistance and services through the Project` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(1) the group may be eligible to receive assistance and services through the Project` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(1) the group may be eligible to receive assistance and services through the Project` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2849 | (2) Participating families, families eligible for or participating in the program authorized under part A of title IV of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.] or the supplemental nutrition assistance program that are assigned to and found eligible for the Project, and families required to submit an application for the Project that are found eligible for the Project shall be ineligible to receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
-- (b)(2): the three kinds of family are ineligible for the supplemental nutrition assistance program; any other is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(2) the family may receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(2) the family may receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(2) the family may receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(2) the family may receive benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(b)(3) Value of assistance`
-- src:2850 | (3)
-- src:2851 | (A) Subject to the provisions of this paragraph and any reduction imposed under subsection (c)(3) of this section, the value of assistance provided to participating families shall not be less than the aggregate value of the assistance such families could receive under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV of the Social Security Act if such families did not participate in the Project.
-- value, aggregate value, reduction under (c)(3): "shall not be less than the aggregate value", less the reduction.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(A) the value of the assistance is enough` 100 100 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(A) the value of the assistance is enough` 150 100 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(A) the value of the assistance is enough` 99 100 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(A) the value of the assistance is enough` 90 100 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(A) the value of the assistance is enough` 89 100 10 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(A) the value of the assistance is enough` 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- src:2852 | (B) For purposes of satisfying the requirement specified in subparagraph (A)—
-- src:2853 | (i) payments for child care expenses under the Project shall be considered part of the value of assistance provided to participating families with earnings;
-- src:2854 | (ii) payments for child care expenses for families without earnings shall not be considered part of the value of assistance provided to participating families or the aggregate value of assistance that such families could have received under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV of the Social Security Act; and
-- src:2855 | (iii) any child support payments not assigned to the State under the provisions of part A of title IV of the Social Security Act, less $50 per month, shall be considered part of the aggregate value of assistance participating families would receive if such families did not participate in the Project;
-- other assistance, child care payments, family has earnings: (i) counts child care for a family with earnings, (ii) not for one without.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(B) the value of assistance provided, counting child care as the text counts it, in dollars` 200 50 TRUE EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(B) the value of assistance provided, counting child care as the text counts it, in dollars` 200 50 FALSE EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(B) the value of assistance provided, counting child care as the text counts it, in dollars` 0 0 FALSE EQUALS 0
-- (iii): child support not assigned to the State, less $50 per month.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(B)(iii) the child support counted in the aggregate value for a month, in dollars` 80 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(B)(iii) the child support counted in the aggregate value for a month, in dollars` 50 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(B)(iii) the child support counted in the aggregate value for a month, in dollars` 49 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(B)(iii) the child support counted in the aggregate value for a month, in dollars` 51 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(B)(iii) the child support counted in the aggregate value for a month, in dollars` 0 EQUALS 0
-- src:2857 | (i) identify the sets of characteristics indicative of families that might receive less assistance under the Project;
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(C)(i) the State has identified the sets of characteristics` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(C)(i) the State has identified the sets of characteristics` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2856 | (C) For purposes of satisfying the requirement specified in subparagraph (A), the State shall—
-- src:2857 | (i) identify the sets of characteristics indicative of families that might receive less assistance under the Project;
-- src:2858 | (ii) establish a mechanism to determine, for each participating family that has a set of characteristics identified under clause (i) whether such family could receive more assistance, in the aggregate, under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV of the Social Security Act if such family did not participate in the project;
-- src:2859 | (iii) increase the amount of assistance provided under the Project to any family that could receive more assistance, in the aggregate, under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV of the Social Security Act if such family did not participate in the Project, so that the assistance provided under the Project to such family is not less than the aggregate amount of assistance such family could receive under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and part A of title IV of the Social Security Act if such family did not participate in the Project; and
-- src:2860 | (iv) increase the amount of assistance paid to participating families, if the State or locality imposes a sales tax on food, by the amount needed to compensate for the tax.
-- src:2861 | This subparagraph shall not be construed to require the State to make the determination under clause (ii) for families that do not have a set of characteristics identified under clause (i).
-- (C)(ii) and the last sentence: the determination is for families with a set of characteristics identified under clause (i), not others.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(C) the State shall make the determination for the family` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(C) the State shall make the determination for the family` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (C)(iii): the aggregate amount against the assistance provided.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iii) the increase the State shall make in the assistance, in dollars` 300 250 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iii) the increase the State shall make in the assistance, in dollars` 250 250 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iii) the increase the State shall make in the assistance, in dollars` 200 250 EQUALS 0
-- (C)(iv): the sales tax.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iv) the State shall increase the amount of assistance paid to participating families for the sales tax` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iv) the State shall increase the amount of assistance paid to participating families for the sales tax` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iv) the increase for the sales tax, in dollars` TRUE 12 EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(C)(iv) the increase for the sales tax, in dollars` FALSE 12 EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2862 | (D)
-- src:2863 | (i) The State shall designate standardized amounts of assistance provided as food assistance under the Project and notify monthly each participating family of such designated amount.
-- src:2864 | (ii) The amount of food assistance so designated shall be at least the value of benefits such family could have received under the supplemental nutrition assistance program if the Project had not been implemented. The provisions of this subparagraph shall not require that the State make individual determinations as to the amount of assistance under the Project designated as food assistance.
-- src:2865 | (iii) The State shall periodically allow participating families the option to receive such food assistance in the form of benefits.
-- (D)(ii): designated food assistance, value of the benefits: "at least".
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(D)(ii) the designated food assistance is enough` 100 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(D)(ii) the designated food assistance is enough` 101 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(D)(ii) the designated food assistance is enough` 99 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:2863 | (i) The State shall designate standardized amounts of assistance provided as food assistance under the Project and notify monthly each participating family of such designated amount.
-- (D)(i): the amounts designated and the family notified this month.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(D)(i) the State has designated the amounts and notified the family` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(D)(i) the State has designated the amounts and notified the family` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(D)(i) the State has designated the amounts and notified the family` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(D)(i) the State has designated the amounts and notified the family` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2865 | (iii) The State shall periodically allow participating families the option to receive such food assistance in the form of benefits.
-- (D)(iii): the option to receive the food assistance as benefits.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(D)(iii) the State has allowed the family the option` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(D)(iii) the State has allowed the family the option` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2867 | (i) Individuals ineligible for the Project who are members of a household including a participating family shall have their eligibility for the supplemental nutrition assistance program determined and have their benefits calculated and issued following the standards established under the supplemental nutrition assistance program, except as provided differently in this subparagraph.
-- (E)(i): an individual ineligible for the Project who is a member of a household including a participating family.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(i) the individual's eligibility and benefits follow the standards of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(i) the individual's eligibility and benefits follow the standards of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(i) the individual's eligibility and benefits follow the standards of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2868 | (ii) The State agency shall determine such individuals’ eligibility for benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program and the amount of such benefits without regard to the participating family.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(ii) the State agency determined the individual's eligibility and benefits without regard to the participating family` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(ii) the State agency determined the individual's eligibility and benefits without regard to the participating family` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(ii) the State agency determined the individual's eligibility and benefits without regard to the participating family` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2869 | (iii) In computing such individuals’ income for purposes of determining eligibility (under section 2014(c)(1) of this title) and benefits, the State agency shall apply the maximum excess shelter expense deduction specified under section 2014(e) of this title.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iii) the State agency applied the maximum excess shelter expense deduction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iii) the State agency applied the maximum excess shelter expense deduction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iii) the State agency applied the maximum excess shelter expense deduction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2870 | (iv) Such individuals’ monthly allotment shall be the higher of $10 or 75 percent of the amount calculated following the standards of the supplemental nutrition assistance program and the foregoing requirements of this subparagraph, rounded to the nearest lower whole dollar.
-- (E)(iv): "the higher of $10 or 75 percent of the amount calculated ..., rounded to the nearest lower whole dollar".
-- 75 percent of 100 is 75; of 101 is 75.75, rounded down 75.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, in dollars` TRUE (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 75
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, in dollars` TRUE (JUST 101) EQUALS JUST 75
-- 75 percent of 13 is 9.75, so $10 is the higher; of 14 is 10.5, rounded down 10; of 15 is 11.25, rounded down 11; of 0 is 0.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, in dollars` TRUE (JUST 13) EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, in dollars` TRUE (JUST 14) EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, in dollars` TRUE (JUST 15) EQUALS JUST 11
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, in dollars` TRUE (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 10
-- the amount calculated by the standards of the supplemental nutrition assistance program was not supplied, or the person is outside (E).
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, in dollars` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, in dollars` FALSE (JUST 100) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, in dollars` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- fork FR-31-1: rounding after taking the higher gives the same answer, since $10 is a whole number.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, rounding after taking the higher, in dollars` 100 EQUALS 75
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, rounding after taking the higher, in dollars` 101 EQUALS 75
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, rounding after taking the higher, in dollars` 13 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, rounding after taking the higher, in dollars` 14 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, rounding after taking the higher, in dollars` 15 EQUALS 11
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, rounding after taking the higher, in dollars` 0 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(3)(E)(iv) the individual's monthly allotment, rounding after taking the higher, in dollars` 1000 EQUALS 750

§§ `(b)(4) and (b)(5) Services; selection`
-- src:2871 | (4) The Project shall include education, employment, and training services equivalent to those offered under the employment and training program described in section 2015(d)(4) of this title to families similar to participating families elsewhere in the State.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(4) the Project includes the education, employment, and training services it shall include` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(4) the Project includes the education, employment, and training services it shall include` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2872 | (5) The State may select families for participation in the Project through submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project or by assigning to the Project families that are determined eligible for or are participating in the program authorized by part A of title IV of the Social Security Act or the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(5) the State may select a family this way` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(5) the State may select a family this way` `s 2031 by assigning a family determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(5) the State may select a family this way` `s 2031 in some other way` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(b)(6) Selection through an application`
-- src:2873 | (6) Whenever selection for participation in the Project is accomplished through submission and approval of an application for the Project—
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6) selection is accomplished through submission and approval of an application` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6) selection is accomplished through submission and approval of an application` `s 2031 by assigning a family determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6) selection is accomplished through submission and approval of an application` `s 2031 in some other way` EQUALS FALSE
-- src:2874 | (A) the State shall promptly determine eligibility for the Project, and issue assistance to eligible families, retroactive to the date of application, not later than thirty days following the family’s filing of an application;
-- (A): done, days from filing: thirty days is in time, thirty-one is not.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(A) the State agency determined eligibility and issued assistance in time` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` TRUE 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(A) the State agency determined eligibility and issued assistance in time` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(A) the State agency determined eligibility and issued assistance in time` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` TRUE 31 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not yet done: past thirty days it is late, within thirty it is open.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(A) the State agency determined eligibility and issued assistance in time` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` FALSE 31 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(A) the State agency determined eligibility and issued assistance in time` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` FALSE 30 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(A) the State agency determined eligibility and issued assistance in time` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` FALSE 10 EQUALS NOTHING
-- another way of selecting: the lead-in of (6) is not met.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(A) the State agency determined eligibility and issued assistance in time` `s 2031 by assigning a family determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program` TRUE 10 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(A) the State agency determined eligibility and issued assistance in time` `s 2031 in some other way` FALSE 99 EQUALS NOTHING
-- "retroactive to the date of application".
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(A) the date to which the assistance to an eligible family is retroactive` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` (Date 5 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 5 3 2025)
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(A) the date to which the assistance to an eligible family is retroactive` `s 2031 by assigning a family determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program` (Date 5 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2875 | (B) in the case of families determined ineligible for the Project upon application, the application for the Project shall be deemed an application for the supplemental nutrition assistance program, and benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall be issued to those found eligible following the standards established under the supplemental nutrition assistance program;
-- (B): ineligible upon application, and then whether found eligible under the standards of the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(B) the application is deemed an application for the supplemental nutrition assistance program` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(B) the application is deemed an application for the supplemental nutrition assistance program` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(B) the application is deemed an application for the supplemental nutrition assistance program` `s 2031 by assigning a family determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(B) benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall be issued to the family` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(B) benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall be issued to the family` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(B) benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall be issued to the family` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(B) benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall be issued to the family` `s 2031 by submission and approval of an application for participation in the Project` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(6)(B) benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall be issued to the family` `s 2031 by assigning a family determined eligible for or participating in the part A of title IV program or the supplemental nutrition assistance program` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2876 | (C) expedited benefits shall be provided under terms no more restrictive than under paragraph (9) of section 2020(e) of this title and the laws of Minnesota and shall include expedited issuance of designated food assistance provided through the Project or expedited benefits through the supplemental nutrition assistance program;
-- (C): expedited benefits no more restrictive than section 2020(e)(9); the Minnesota laws are not in this text.
