#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(13) the State has carried out the supplemental nutrition assistance program as the text requires` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2898 | (A) Except as provided in subparagraph (B), the State will carry out the Project during a five-year period beginning on the date the first family receives assistance under the Project.
-- (14)(A): a five-year period beginning on the date the first family receives assistance; the last day is the day before the fifth anniversary (fork FR-31-4).
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(14)(A) the last day of the five-year period` (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS (Date 31 5 2030)
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(14)(A) the last day of the five-year period` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS (Date 31 12 2029)
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(14)(A) the last day of the five-year period` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS (Date 30 12 2030)
-- a period begun on 29 February 2024 ends on 28 February 2029 (no 29 February 2029), and one begun on 1 March 2024 ends on the same day.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(14)(A) the last day of the five-year period` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS (Date 28 2 2029)
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(14)(A) the last day of the five-year period` (Date 1 3 2024) EQUALS (Date 28 2 2029)
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(14)(A) the day falls in the five-year period` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(14)(A) the day falls in the five-year period` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 31 5 2030) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(14)(A) the day falls in the five-year period` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 1 6 2030) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(14)(A) the day falls in the five-year period` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 31 5 2025) EQUALS FALSE
-- src:2899 | (B) The Project may be terminated—
-- src:2900 | (i) by the State one hundred and eighty days after the State gives notice to the Secretary that it intends to terminate the Project;
-- src:2901 | (ii) by the Secretary one hundred and eighty days after the Secretary, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing, determines that the State materially failed to comply with this section; or
-- src:2902 | (iii) whenever the State and the Secretary jointly agree to terminate the Project.
-- (14)(B): (i) the State, 180 days after the notice: 1 January 2026 plus 180 days is 30 June 2026; 15 August 2025 plus 180 days is 11 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(14)(B) the first day on which the Project may be terminated` `s 2031 the State, on notice to the Secretary` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 30 6 2026)
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(14)(B) the first day on which the Project may be terminated` `s 2031 the State, on notice to the Secretary` (Date 15 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 11 2 2026)
-- (ii) the Secretary, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing; without them, not covered.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(14)(B) the first day on which the Project may be terminated` `s 2031 the Secretary, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing, on finding that the State materially failed to comply` (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 30 6 2026)
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(14)(B) the first day on which the Project may be terminated` `s 2031 the Secretary, after notice and an opportunity for a hearing, on finding that the State materially failed to comply` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (iii) whenever the State and the Secretary jointly agree: the day of the agreement.
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(14)(B) the first day on which the Project may be terminated` `s 2031 the State and the Secretary jointly agree` (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2026)
-- src:2903 | (15) Not more than six thousand families may participate in the Project simultaneously.
