#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(15) the number of families participating simultaneously is within the limit` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(b)(15) the number of families participating simultaneously is within the limit` 6001 EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `(c) Additional terms and conditions of Project`
-- src:2906 | (1) The State may require any parent in a participating family to participate in education, employment, or training requirements unless the individual is a parent in a family with one parent who—
-- src:2907 | (A) is ill, incapacitated, or sixty years of age or older;
-- src:2908 | (B) is needed in the home because of the illness or incapacity of another family member;
-- src:2909 | (C) is the parent of a child under one year of age and is personally providing care for the child;
-- src:2910 | (D) is the parent of a child under six years of age and is employed or participating in education or employment and training services for twenty or more hours a week;
-- src:2911 | (E) works thirty or more hours a week or, if the number of hours worked cannot be verified, earns at least the Federal minimum hourly wage rate multiplied by thirty per week; or
-- src:2912 | (F) is in the second or third trimester of pregnancy.
-- (c)(1): the parent's fields, in order: one parent; ill or incapacitated; age; needed in the home; age in months of the youngest child (-1 for none);
-- personally provides care; hours a week employed or in education or training; hours verifiable; hours worked; earnings a week; trimester.
-- A one-parent family and a parent with no exemption: the State may require participation.
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 120, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (A) ill, incapacitated, or sixty or older: sixty is exempt, fifty-nine is not.
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, TRUE, 30, FALSE, 120, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 60, FALSE, 120, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 59, FALSE, 120, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (B) needed in the home because of the illness or incapacity of another family member.
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, TRUE, 120, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (C) a child under one year (twelve months) and personally providing care: eleven months and caring is exempt; eleven months not caring, and twelve months, are not.
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 11, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 0, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 11, FALSE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 12, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (D) a child under six years (seventy-two months) and twenty or more hours a week: 71 months and 20 hours is exempt; 19 hours, and 72 months, are not.
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 71, FALSE, 20, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 71, FALSE, 19, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 72, FALSE, 20, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no child at all: (C) and (D) do not apply however many hours.
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, (0 MINUS 1), TRUE, 40, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (E) thirty or more hours worked, or, if they cannot be verified, earnings of at least the Federal minimum hourly wage rate (7.25) times thirty (217.50).
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 120, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 30, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 120, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 29, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 120, TRUE, 10, FALSE, 0, 217.5, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 120, TRUE, 10, FALSE, 0, 217.49, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- hours that cannot be verified are not counted, and earnings count only when they cannot; a higher wage rate raises the bar.
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 120, TRUE, 10, FALSE, 40, 0, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 120, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 1000, 0) 7.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 120, TRUE, 10, FALSE, 0, 217.5, 0) 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (F) second or third trimester of pregnancy.
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 120, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 2) 7.25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 120, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 3) 7.25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 120, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 1) 7.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the exemptions are for "a family with one parent": a parent in a family of two parents is not exempt on any of them.
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(1) the State may require the parent to participate in education, employment, or training requirements` (`s 2031 parent` OF FALSE, TRUE, 65, TRUE, 5, TRUE, 40, TRUE, 40, 0, 3) 7.25 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- src:2913 | (2) The State shall not require any parent of a child under six years of age in a participating family with only one parent to be employed or participate in education or employment and training services for more than twenty hours a week.
-- (c)(2): a one-parent family whose youngest child is under six: more than twenty hours is barred; twenty or fewer is not covered here.
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(2) the State may require the parent to be employed or participate for the hours` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 60, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 21 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(2) the State may require the parent to be employed or participate for the hours` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 60, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 20 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(2) the State may require the parent to be employed or participate for the hours` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 60, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(2) the State may require the parent to be employed or participate for the hours` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 0, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 21 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(2) the State may require the parent to be employed or participate for the hours` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 71, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a family of two parents, a child of six or more, or no child: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(2) the State may require the parent to be employed or participate for the hours` (`s 2031 parent` OF FALSE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 60, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 40 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(2) the State may require the parent to be employed or participate for the hours` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, 72, TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 40 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(2) the State may require the parent to be employed or participate for the hours` (`s 2031 parent` OF TRUE, FALSE, 30, FALSE, (0 MINUS 1), TRUE, 10, TRUE, 10, 0, 0) 40 EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2914 | (3) For any period during which an individual required to participate in education, employment, or training requirements fails to comply without good cause with a requirement imposed by the State under paragraph (1), the amount of assistance to the family under the Project may be reduced by an amount not more than 10 percent of the assistance the family would be eligible for with no income other than that from the Project.
-- (c)(3): required, fails to comply without good cause; the reduction is not more than 10 percent of the assistance with no other income.
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(3) the most the assistance to the family may be reduced by, in dollars` TRUE TRUE 500 EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(3) the most the assistance to the family may be reduced by, in dollars` TRUE TRUE 333 EQUALS JUST 33.3
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(3) the most the assistance to the family may be reduced by, in dollars` TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(3) the most the assistance to the family may be reduced by, in dollars` TRUE FALSE 500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(3) the most the assistance to the family may be reduced by, in dollars` FALSE TRUE 500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(3) the assistance to the family may be reduced by the amount` TRUE TRUE 500 50 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(3) the assistance to the family may be reduced by the amount` TRUE TRUE 500 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(3) the assistance to the family may be reduced by the amount` TRUE TRUE 500 50.01 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(3) the assistance to the family may be reduced by the amount` TRUE TRUE 500 51 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(3) the assistance to the family may be reduced by the amount` TRUE FALSE 500 10 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(c)(3) the assistance to the family may be reduced by the amount` FALSE FALSE 500 10 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(d) Funding`
-- src:2916 | (1) If an application submitted under subsection (a) complies with the requirements specified in subsection (b), then the Secretary shall—
-- src:2917 | (A) approve such application; and
-- (d)(1)(A): a complying application ("If ... complies ..., then the Secretary shall approve").
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(A) the Secretary shall approve the application` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(A) the Secretary shall approve the application` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(A) the Secretary shall approve the application` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2918 | (B) subject to subsection (b)(12) from the funds appropriated under this chapter provide grant awards and pay the State each calendar quarter for—
-- src:2919 | (i) the cost of food assistance provided under the Project equal to the amount that would have otherwise been issued in the form of benefits under the supplemental nutrition assistance program had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary after negotiations with the State; and
-- src:2920 | (ii) the administrative costs incurred by the State to provide food assistance under the Project that are authorized under subsections (a), (g), (h)(2), and (h)(3) of section 2025 of this title equal to the amount that otherwise would have been paid under such subsections had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary after negotiations with the State: Provided, That payments made under subsection (g) of section 2025 of this title shall equal payments that would have been made if the Project had not been implemented.
-- (d)(1)(B)(i): the amount that would have been issued as benefits, "subject to subsection (b)(12)".
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(B)(i) the payment for the cost of food assistance, in dollars` 1000 5000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(B)(i) the payment for the cost of food assistance, in dollars` 5000 5000 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(B)(i) the payment for the cost of food assistance, in dollars` 6000 5000 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(B)(i) the payment for the cost of food assistance, in dollars` 0 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(B)(i) the payment for the cost of food assistance, in dollars` 100 0 EQUALS 0
-- (d)(1)(B)(ii): the administrative costs incurred, equal to the amount that otherwise would have been paid (fork FR-31-8).
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(B)(ii) the payment for administrative costs, in dollars` (JUST 800) 1000 EQUALS JUST 800
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(B)(ii) the payment for administrative costs, in dollars` (JUST 800) 700 EQUALS JUST 700
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(B)(ii) the payment for administrative costs, in dollars` (JUST 800) 800 EQUALS JUST 800
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(B)(ii) the payment for administrative costs, in dollars` NOTHING 700 EQUALS NOTHING
-- the proviso: payments under subsection (g) of section 2025 "shall equal" what would have been made.
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(B)(ii) the payments under subsection (g) of section 2025 are as the proviso requires` 500 500 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(B)(ii) the payments under subsection (g) of section 2025 are as the proviso requires` 499 500 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(1)(B)(ii) the payments under subsection (g) of section 2025 are as the proviso requires` 501 500 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:2922 | (A) the cost of benefits issued to individuals ineligible for the Project specified in subsection (b)(3)(E) in excess of the amount that would have been issued to such individuals had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary after negotiations with the State; and
-- src:2923 | (B) the cost of benefits issued to families exercising the option specified in subsection (b)(3)(D)(iii) in excess of the amount that would have been issued to such individuals had the Project not been implemented, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary after negotiations with the State.
-- (d)(2)(A) and (B): the cost of benefits issued "in excess of the amount that would have been issued", and nothing for no excess.
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(2)(A) the adjustment for benefits issued to individuals ineligible for the Project, in dollars` 120 100 EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(2)(A) the adjustment for benefits issued to individuals ineligible for the Project, in dollars` 100 100 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(2)(A) the adjustment for benefits issued to individuals ineligible for the Project, in dollars` 80 100 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(2)(B) the adjustment for benefits issued to families exercising the option, in dollars` 120 100 EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(2)(B) the adjustment for benefits issued to families exercising the option, in dollars` 100 100 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(2)(B) the adjustment for benefits issued to families exercising the option, in dollars` 80 100 EQUALS 0
-- src:2924 | (3) Payments under paragraph (1)(B) shall include adjustments, as estimated under a methodology satisfactory to the Secretary after negotiations with the State, for increases or decreases in the costs of providing food assistance and associated administrative costs that result from changes in economic, demographic, or other conditions in the State based on data specific to the State, changes in eligibility or benefit levels authorized by this chapter, and changes in or additional amounts of Federal funds available to States and localities under the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
-- (d)(3): the payment includes adjustments for increases or decreases.
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(3) the payment under paragraph (1)(B) including the adjustments, in dollars` 1000 50 EQUALS 1050
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(3) the payment under paragraph (1)(B) including the adjustments, in dollars` 1000 (0 MINUS 50) EQUALS 950
#ASSERT `s 2031(d)(3) the payment under paragraph (1)(B) including the adjustments, in dollars` 0 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `(e) Waiver`
-- src:2926 | With respect to the Project, the Secretary shall waive compliance with any requirement contained in this chapter (other than this section) that, if applied, would prevent the State from carrying out the Project or effectively achieving its purpose.
-- the requirement is in this section; the requirement would prevent the State from carrying out the Project.
#ASSERT `s 2031(e) the Secretary shall waive compliance with the requirement` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(e) the Secretary shall waive compliance with the requirement` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(e) the Secretary shall waive compliance with the requirement` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(e) the Secretary shall waive compliance with the requirement` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(f) Project audits`
-- src:2928 | The Comptroller General of the United States shall—
-- src:2929 | (1) conduct periodic audits of the operation of the Project to verify the amounts payable to the State from time to time under subsection (d); and
#ASSERT `s 2031(f)(1) the Comptroller General has conducted the audits the text requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(f)(1) the Comptroller General has conducted the audits the text requires` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2930 | (2) submit to the Secretary, the Secretary of Health and Human Services, the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives, and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate a report describing the results of each such audit.
-- the four recipients: the Secretary; the Secretary of Health and Human Services; the House Committee; the Senate Committee.
#ASSERT `s 2031(f)(2) the Comptroller General has submitted the report of the audit to all four recipients` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(f)(2) the Comptroller General has submitted the report of the audit to all four recipients` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(f)(2) the Comptroller General has submitted the report of the audit to all four recipients` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(f)(2) the Comptroller General has submitted the report of the audit to all four recipients` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(f)(2) the Comptroller General has submitted the report of the audit to all four recipients` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(g) Construction`
-- src:2932 | (1) For purposes of any Federal, State, or local law other than part A of title IV of the Social Security Act [42 U.S.C. 601 et seq.] or this chapter—
-- src:2933 | (A) cash assistance provided under the Project that is designated as food assistance by the State shall be treated in the same manner as benefits allotments under the supplemental nutrition assistance program are treated; and
-- the law is part A of title IV or this chapter (then the paragraph does not speak); cash assistance designated as food assistance.
#ASSERT `s 2031(g)(1)(A) the cash assistance is treated in the same manner as benefit allotments under the supplemental nutrition assistance program` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(g)(1)(A) the cash assistance is treated in the same manner as benefit allotments under the supplemental nutrition assistance program` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(g)(1)(A) the cash assistance is treated in the same manner as benefit allotments under the supplemental nutrition assistance program` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(g)(1)(A) the cash assistance is treated in the same manner as benefit allotments under the supplemental nutrition assistance program` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2934 | (B) participating families shall be treated in the same manner as participants in the supplemental nutrition assistance program are treated.
#ASSERT `s 2031(g)(1)(B) the family is treated in the same manner as a participant in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(g)(1)(B) the family is treated in the same manner as a participant in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(g)(1)(B) the family is treated in the same manner as a participant in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(g)(1)(B) the family is treated in the same manner as a participant in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2935 | (2) Nothing in this section shall—
-- src:2936 | (A) allow payments made to the State under the Project to be less than the amounts the State and eligible households within the State would have received if the Project had not been implemented; or
-- (g)(2)(A): payments less than the amounts they would have been are not allowed; at or above is not touched.
#ASSERT `s 2031(g)(2)(A) this section allows the payments made to the State` 99 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(g)(2)(A) this section allows the payments made to the State` 100 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(g)(2)(A) this section allows the payments made to the State` 101 100 EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2937 | (B) require the Secretary to incur costs as a result of the Project in excess of costs that would have been incurred if the Project had not been implemented, except for costs for evaluation.
-- (g)(2)(B): costs in excess of what would have been incurred are not required.
#ASSERT `s 2031(g)(2)(B) this section requires the Secretary to incur the costs` 101 100 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(g)(2)(B) this section requires the Secretary to incur the costs` 100 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(g)(2)(B) this section requires the Secretary to incur the costs` 99 100 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(h) Quality control`
-- src:2939 | Participating families shall be excluded from any sample taken for purposes of making any determination under section 2025(c) of this title. For purposes of establishing the total value of allotments under section 2025(c)(1) of this title, benefits and the amount of federal liability for food assistance provided under the Project as limited by subsection (b)(12) of this section shall be treated as allotments issued under the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
#ASSERT `s 2031(h) the family is excluded from the sample` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(h) the family is excluded from the sample` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the total value of allotments: allotments, plus benefits, plus the federal liability as limited by (b)(12) (fork FR-31-10).
#ASSERT `s 2031(h) the total value of allotments under section 2025(c)(1), in dollars` 1000 100 500 800 EQUALS 1600
#ASSERT `s 2031(h) the total value of allotments under section 2025(c)(1), in dollars` 1000 100 900 800 EQUALS 1900
#ASSERT `s 2031(h) the total value of allotments under section 2025(c)(1), in dollars` 1000 0 800 800 EQUALS 1800
#ASSERT `s 2031(h) the total value of allotments under section 2025(c)(1), in dollars` 0 0 0 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `(i) Evaluation`
-- src:2941 | (1) The State shall develop and implement a plan for an independent evaluation designed to provide reliable information on Project impacts and implementation. The evaluation will include treatment and control groups and will include random assignment of families to treatment and control groups in an urban setting. The evaluation plan shall satisfy the evaluation concerns of the Secretary of Agriculture such as effects on benefits to participants, costs of the Project, payment accuracy, administrative consequences, any reduction in welfare dependency, any reduction in total assistance payments, and the consequences of cash payments on household expenditures, and food consumption. The evaluation plan shall take into consideration the evaluation requirements and administrative obligations of the State. The evaluation will measure the effects of the Project in regard to goals of increasing family income, prevention of long-term dependency, movement toward self-support, and simplification of the welfare system.
-- the plan's five fields, in order: independent evaluation; treatment and control groups with random assignment in an urban setting;
-- satisfies the evaluation concerns of the Secretary of Agriculture; takes into consideration the State's requirements; measures the effects on the four goals.
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the plan contains what the text requires` (`s 2031 evaluation plan` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the plan contains what the text requires` (`s 2031 evaluation plan` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the plan contains what the text requires` (`s 2031 evaluation plan` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the plan contains what the text requires` (`s 2031 evaluation plan` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the plan contains what the text requires` (`s 2031 evaluation plan` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the plan contains what the text requires` (`s 2031 evaluation plan` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- "such as ...": the eight concerns named, and "such as" leaves the list open.
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the concern is one the evaluation plan shall satisfy` `s 2031 effects on benefits to participants` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the concern is one the evaluation plan shall satisfy` `s 2031 costs of the Project` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the concern is one the evaluation plan shall satisfy` `s 2031 payment accuracy` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the concern is one the evaluation plan shall satisfy` `s 2031 administrative consequences` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the concern is one the evaluation plan shall satisfy` `s 2031 any reduction in welfare dependency` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the concern is one the evaluation plan shall satisfy` `s 2031 any reduction in total assistance payments` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the concern is one the evaluation plan shall satisfy` `s 2031 the consequences of cash payments on household expenditures` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the concern is one the evaluation plan shall satisfy` `s 2031 the consequences of cash payments on food consumption` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(1) the concern is one the evaluation plan shall satisfy` `s 2031 some other concern` EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2942 | (2) The State shall pay 50 percent of the cost of developing and implementing such plan and the Federal Government shall pay the remainder.
-- (i)(2): the State pays 50 percent of the cost and the Federal Government the remainder.
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(2) the State's share of the cost of the plan, in dollars` 1000 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(2) the Federal Government's share of the cost of the plan, in dollars` 1000 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(2) the State's share of the cost of the plan, in dollars` 333 EQUALS 166.5
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(2) the Federal Government's share of the cost of the plan, in dollars` 333 EQUALS 166.5
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(2) the State's share of the cost of the plan, in dollars` 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 2031(i)(2) the Federal Government's share of the cost of the plan, in dollars` 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `(j) Definitions`
-- src:2945 | (1) The term “family” means the following individuals who live together: a minor child or a group of minor children related to each other as siblings, half siblings, stepsiblings, or adopted siblings, together with their natural or adoptive parents, or their caregiver. Family also includes a pregnant woman in the third trimester of pregnancy with no children.
-- (j)(1): the group's fields, in order: live together; number of minor children; related as siblings, half siblings, stepsiblings or adopted siblings;
-- a natural or adoptive parent lives with them; the children's caregiver lives with them; a pregnant woman in the third trimester with no children.
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(1) the group is a family` (`s 2031 group` OF TRUE, 1, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(1) the group is a family` (`s 2031 group` OF TRUE, 2, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(1) the group is a family` (`s 2031 group` OF TRUE, 2, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(1) the group is a family` (`s 2031 group` OF TRUE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(1) the group is a family` (`s 2031 group` OF FALSE, 0, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- children who are not siblings; do not live together; no children (adults only).
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(1) the group is a family` (`s 2031 group` OF TRUE, 2, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(1) the group is a family` (`s 2031 group` OF FALSE, 1, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(1) the group is a family` (`s 2031 group` OF TRUE, 0, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- minor children living together with neither a parent nor a caregiver: the text does not say (fork FR-31-6).
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(1) the group is a family` (`s 2031 group` OF TRUE, 1, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(1) the group is a family` (`s 2031 group` OF TRUE, 2, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:2946 | (2) The term “contract” means a plan to help a family pursue self-sufficiency, based on the State’s assessment of the family’s needs and abilities and developed with a parental caregiver.
-- (j)(2): a plan to help a family pursue self-sufficiency; based on the State's assessment; developed with a parental caregiver (undefined here).
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(2) the document is a contract` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(2) the document is a contract` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(2) the document is a contract` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(2) the document is a contract` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(2) the document is a contract` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(2) the document is a contract` FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:2947 | (3) The term “caregiver” means a minor child’s natural or adoptive parent or parents who live in the home with the minor child. For purposes of determining eligibility for the Project, “caregiver” also means any of the following individuals who live with and provide care and support to a minor child when the minor child’s natural or adoptive parent or parents do not reside in the same home: grandfather, grandmother, brother, sister, stepfather, stepmother, stepbrother, stepsister, uncle, aunt, first cousin, nephew, niece, persons of preceding generations as denoted by prefixes of “great” or “great-great” or a spouse of any person named in the above groups even after the marriage ends by death or divorce.
-- (j)(3), first sentence: a natural or adoptive parent who lives in the home with the minor child. The inputs, in order after the relationship:
-- lives in the home with the child; provides care and support; a natural or adoptive parent resides in the same home; the purpose is determining eligibility.
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 natural or adoptive parent` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 natural or adoptive parent` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 natural or adoptive parent` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- second sentence, for purposes of determining eligibility: a listed relative who lives with and provides care and support when no parent resides in the home.
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 grandfather` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 grandmother` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 brother` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 sister` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 stepfather` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 stepmother` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 stepbrother` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 stepsister` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 uncle` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 aunt` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 first cousin` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 nephew` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 niece` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 a person of a preceding generation denoted by the prefix great or great-great` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 a spouse of any person named above, even after the marriage ends by death or divorce` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the same relatives fail when a parent resides in the same home, when the person does not live with or care for the child,
-- when the purpose is not determining eligibility, and for any other relationship.
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 grandfather` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 grandfather` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 grandfather` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 grandfather` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(3) the person is a caregiver` `s 2031 some other relationship` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- src:2948 | (4) The term “State” means the State of Minnesota.
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(4) the name is the State` "Minnesota" EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(4) the name is the State` "Wisconsin" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(4) the name is the State` "minnesota" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2031(j)(4) the name is the State` "" EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Regulative rules, run with #TRACE`
-- The stable binary does not let #ASSERT take a #TRACE outcome, so each trace states the outcome it should print.
-- src:2874 | (A) the State shall promptly determine eligibility for the Project, and issue assistance to eligible families, retroactive to the date of application, not later than thirty days following the family’s filing of an application;
-- (b)(6)(A): the State agency determines and issues assistance on day 20. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 2031(b)(6)(A) the State agency's duty to determine eligibility and issue assistance` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State agency` DOES `s 2031 determine eligibility for the Project and issue assistance to eligible families` AT 20
-- (b)(6)(A): on day 30. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 2031(b)(6)(A) the State agency's duty to determine eligibility and issue assistance` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State agency` DOES `s 2031 determine eligibility for the Project and issue assistance to eligible families` AT 30
-- (b)(6)(A): nothing by day 31. Expected: BREACH BY the State agency.
#TRACE `s 2031(b)(6)(A) the State agency's duty to determine eligibility and issue assistance` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)
-- src:2877 | (D) each individual who contacts the State in person during office hours to make what may reasonably be interpreted as an oral or written request to receive financial assistance shall receive and shall be permitted to file an application form on the same day such contact is first made;
-- (b)(6)(D): the form is given and filing permitted on the day of contact (day 0). Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 2031(b)(6)(D) the State agency's duty to give an application form the same day` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State agency` DOES `s 2031 give the individual an application form and permit its filing` AT 0
-- (b)(6)(D): the next day. Expected: BREACH BY the State agency.
#TRACE `s 2031(b)(6)(D) the State agency's duty to give an application form the same day` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State agency` DOES `s 2031 give the individual an application form and permit its filing` AT 1
-- src:2880 | (i) restrict the number of families who may be represented by such person; and
-- src:2881 | (ii) otherwise establish criteria and verification standards for representation under this subparagraph; and
-- (b)(6)(F)(i) and (ii): the State agency exercises each permission. Expected: FULFILLED each.
#TRACE `s 2031(b)(6)(F)(i) the State agency's permission to restrict the number of families a person may represent` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State agency` DOES `s 2031 restrict the number of families who may be represented by such person` AT 3
#TRACE `s 2031(b)(6)(F)(ii) the State agency's permission to establish criteria and verification standards for representation` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State agency` DOES `s 2031 establish criteria and verification standards for representation` AT 3
-- src:2889 | (A) The State shall provide each family or family member whose participation in the Project ends and each family whose participation is terminated with notice of the existence of the supplemental nutrition assistance program and the person or agency to contact for more information.
-- (b)(10)(A): the State agency gives the notice. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 2031(b)(10)(A) the State agency's duty to give notice of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State agency` DOES `s 2031 notify the family of the supplemental nutrition assistance program and whom to contact` AT 5
-- src:2892 | (ii) If sections 256.031 through 256.036 of the Minnesota Statutes, 1989 Supplement, or Minnesota Laws 1989, chapter 282, article 5, section 130, are amended to reduce or eliminate benefits provided under those sections or restrict the rights of Project applicants or participating families, the State shall exclude from the Project applicants or participating families or individuals affected by such amendments and follow the standards specified in subparagraph (C), except that the State shall continue to pay from State funds an amount equal to the food assistance portion to such families and individuals until the State determines eligibility or ineligibility for the supplemental nutrition assistance program or the family or individual has failed to supply the needed additional information within ten days. Food benefits shall be provided to families and individuals excluded from the Project under this clause who are determined eligible for the supplemental nutrition assistance program retroactive to the date of the determination of eligibility. The Secretary shall pay to the State the value of the benefits for which such families and individuals would have been eligible in the absence of food assistance payments under this clause from the date of termination from the Project to the date benefits are provided.
-- (b)(10)(B)(ii): the State agency continues to pay; the Secretary pays the State. Expected: FULFILLED each.
#TRACE `s 2031(b)(10)(B)(ii) the State agency's duty to continue to pay the food assistance portion` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State agency` DOES `s 2031 continue to pay from State funds an amount equal to the food assistance portion` AT 5
#TRACE `s 2031(b)(10)(B)(ii) the Secretary's duty to pay the State the value of the benefits` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Secretary` DOES `s 2031 pay the State the value of the benefits` AT 5
-- src:2893 | (C) Each family whose Project participation is terminated shall be screened for potential eligibility for the supplemental nutrition assistance program and if the screening indicates potential eligibility, the family or family member shall be given a specific request to supply all additional information needed to determine such eligibility and assistance in completing a signed supplemental nutrition assistance program application including provision of any relevant information obtained by the State for purpose of the Project. If the family or family member supplies such additional information within ten days after receiving the request, the State shall, within five days after the State receives such information, determine whether the family or family member is eligible for the supplemental nutrition assistance program. Each family or family member who is determined through the screening or otherwise to be ineligible for the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall be notified of that determination.
-- (b)(10)(C): the State agency gives the specific request. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 2031(b)(10)(C) the State agency's duty to give the specific request` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State agency` DOES `s 2031 give the family or family member a specific request for the additional information, with assistance in completing a signed application` AT 2
-- (b)(10)(C): the information reaches the State on day 0 and it determines on day 5. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 2031(b)(10)(C) the State agency's duty to determine eligibility after the information is supplied` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State agency` DOES `s 2031 determine whether the family is eligible for the supplemental nutrition assistance program` AT 5
-- (b)(10)(C): day 6. Expected: BREACH BY the State agency.
#TRACE `s 2031(b)(10)(C) the State agency's duty to determine eligibility after the information is supplied` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 6)
-- src:2896 | (13) The State shall carry out the supplemental nutrition assistance program throughout the State while the State carries out the Project.
-- (b)(13): the State agency carries out the supplemental nutrition assistance program throughout the State. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 2031(b)(13) the State agency's duty to carry out the supplemental nutrition assistance program throughout the State` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State agency` DOES `s 2031 carry out the supplemental nutrition assistance program throughout the State` AT 4
-- src:2916 | (1) If an application submitted under subsection (a) complies with the requirements specified in subsection (b), then the Secretary shall—
-- src:2917 | (A) approve such application; and
-- src:2918 | (B) subject to subsection (b)(12) from the funds appropriated under this chapter provide grant awards and pay the State each calendar quarter for—
-- (d)(1)(A), (d)(1)(B), (d)(2): the Secretary approves, pays and adjusts. Expected: FULFILLED each.
#TRACE `s 2031(d)(1)(A) the Secretary's duty to approve the application` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Secretary` DOES `s 2031 approve the application` AT 7
#TRACE `s 2031(d)(1)(B) the Secretary's duty to pay the State each calendar quarter` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Secretary` DOES `s 2031 pay the State each calendar quarter` AT 90
#TRACE `s 2031(d)(2) the Secretary's duty to adjust the payments made to the State` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Secretary` DOES `s 2031 adjust the payments made to the State` AT 90
-- src:2926 | With respect to the Project, the Secretary shall waive compliance with any requirement contained in this chapter (other than this section) that, if applied, would prevent the State from carrying out the Project or effectively achieving its purpose.
-- (e): the Secretary waives compliance. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 2031(e) the Secretary's duty to waive compliance` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Secretary` DOES `s 2031 waive compliance with a requirement of this chapter` AT 10
-- src:2941 | (1) The State shall develop and implement a plan for an independent evaluation designed to provide reliable information on Project impacts and implementation. The evaluation will include treatment and control groups and will include random assignment of families to treatment and control groups in an urban setting. The evaluation plan shall satisfy the evaluation concerns of the Secretary of Agriculture such as effects on benefits to participants, costs of the Project, payment accuracy, administrative consequences, any reduction in welfare dependency, any reduction in total assistance payments, and the consequences of cash payments on household expenditures, and food consumption. The evaluation plan shall take into consideration the evaluation requirements and administrative obligations of the State. The evaluation will measure the effects of the Project in regard to goals of increasing family income, prevention of long-term dependency, movement toward self-support, and simplification of the welfare system.
-- (i)(1): the State agency develops and implements the plan. Expected: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 2031(i)(1) the State agency's duty to develop and implement an evaluation plan` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the State agency` DOES `s 2031 develop and implement a plan for an independent evaluation` AT 60

